    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1703">

                <pb facs="1449" n="1345" xml:id="pg1345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/154.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 503.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-06-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 481 of April
                    29, 1913, wherein I enclosed a copy of the Sublime Porte’s circular note verbale
                    of April 21 [inclosure 3 with said despatch] in regard to the occupation by
                    Ottoman troops of the houses of foreigners at San Stefano, I now have the honor
                    to transmit a copy of the identic note verbale sent by the foreign missions in
                    reply to the said note.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1703-a1.xml" xpointer="d1703-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
